---
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Nav from "../../../components/Nav.astro";
import Footer from "../../../components/Footer.astro";
import "../../../styles/editorial-remix.scss";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const isRealmsMode = import.meta.env.SITE_MODE === "realms";
if (!isRealmsMode) return Astro.redirect("/ml-portfolio/blog/");
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Living Without Fear | Reading Notes | Kosh"
  description="A reading folio on fear, duality, and self-restraint through passages from the Upaniṣads and Mahābhārata."
  image="/images/atmosphere/reading-notes-cover-hq.webp"
  type="article"
  bodyClass="editorial-remix fear-remix"
>
  <Nav />
  <main class="fear-page">
    <header class="fear-hero">
      <figure>
        <img src={base + "images/atmosphere/reading-notes-cover-hq.webp"} alt="A dark film still with a face lit from below and subtitle text about living without fear." loading="eager" decoding="async" />
      </figure>
      <div class="fear-hero__meta"><span>Reading folio · 01</span><span>Fear · duality · restraint</span></div>
      <h1 aria-label="Living without fear"><span>Living</span><em>without</em><span>Fear</span></h1>
      <p class="fear-hero__dek">Two passages on the moment fear enters—and the disciplines through which it loosens its hold.</p>
      <a class="fear-hero__enter" href="#reading">Begin reading ↓</a>
    </header>

    <div class="editorial-marquee" aria-hidden="true">
      <div><span>Dvitīyād vai bhayaṃ bhavati</span><i>§</i><span>Fear arises from a second</span><i>§</i><span>Dvitīyād vai bhayaṃ bhavati</span><i>§</i><span>Fear arises from a second</span><i>§</i></div>
    </div>

    <article class="fear-reading" id="reading">
      <aside class="fear-reading__rail">
        <p>Contents</p>
        <a href="#duality"><span>01</span>Duality</a>
        <a href="#restraint"><span>02</span>Restraint</a>
        <p class="fear-reading__vertical">Kosh · reading notes · Bengaluru</p>
      </aside>

      <div class="fear-reading__body">
        <header class="fear-reading__opening">
          <p>On living without fear</p>
          <blockquote>Fear is not treated here merely as an emotion. It is a relation: a distance imagined between the self and what appears outside it.</blockquote>
        </header>

        <section class="fear-chapter" id="duality">
          <div class="fear-chapter__number">01</div>
          <header>
            <p>Fear arises from duality / separation</p>
            <h2>Bṛhadāraṇyaka<br />Upaniṣad <em>1.4.2</em></h2>
            <span>Śukla Yajurveda tradition</span>
          </header>
          <blockquote class="fear-verse" lang="sa">
            सोऽबिभेत् तस्मादेकाकी बिभेति ।<br />
            स हायमीक्षां चक्रे यन्मदन्यन्नास्ति कस्मान्नु बिभेमीति ।<br />
            तत एवास्य भयं वीयाय ।<br />
            कस्माद्ध्यभेष्यत् । द्वितीयाद्वै भयं भवति ॥
          </blockquote>
          <div class="fear-translation">
            <p>Transliteration</p>
            <div>so’bibhet tasmād ekākī bibheti…<br /><strong>dvitīyād vai bhayaṃ bhavati.</strong></div>
          </div>
          <div class="fear-translation fear-translation--meaning">
            <p>Meaning</p>
            <div>“He was afraid; therefore one who is alone is afraid. Then he reflected: ‘Since there is nothing other than me, what should I fear?’ Then his fear vanished. For what was there to fear? Fear indeed arises from a second.”</div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <figure class="fear-interlude">
          <img src={base + "essays/a-measure-of-days/silent-area.jpeg"} alt="A weathered sign reading Silent Area in a green garden" loading="lazy" />
          <figcaption><span>Interlude</span>Silence is not the absence of fear, but a room in which its shape becomes visible.</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <section class="fear-chapter" id="restraint">
          <div class="fear-chapter__number">02</div>
          <header>
            <p>Fearlessness through self-restraint</p>
            <h2>Mahābhārata<br /><em>12.213.4–5</em></h2>
            <span>Śānti Parva · Mokṣadharma Parva</span>
          </header>
          <p class="fear-verse-label">Verse 4</p>
          <blockquote class="fear-verse" lang="sa">
            दमस्तेजो वर्धयति पवित्रं दम उच्यते ।<br />
            विपाप्मा निर्भयो दान्तः पुरुषो विन्दते महत् ॥ ४ ॥
          </blockquote>
          <div class="fear-translation">
            <p>IAST</p>
            <div>damaḥ tejo vardhayati pavitraṃ dama ucyate |<br />vipāpmā nirbhayo dāntaḥ puruṣo vindate mahat || 4 ||</div>
          </div>
          <div class="fear-translation fear-translation--meaning">
            <p>Meaning</p>
            <div>“Self-restraint increases one’s energy; self-restraint is said to be purifying. The self-restrained person, free from sin and fearless, attains greatness.”</div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <footer class="fear-colophon">
          <span>§</span>
          <p>A note remains provisional: an invitation to return to the source, compare translations, and resist turning a passage into a slogan.</p>
          <a href={base + "blog/notes/"}>Return to the field notes →</a>
        </footer>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
